# Rocdown site configuration

Place `rocdown.toml` at the documentation content root when you need site
metadata, hashed assets, or curated navigation. The file is optional: a
directory of `.rocdown` pages is enough for `rocdown check`,
`rocdown build`, and `rocdown view`.

```toml
[site]
title = "My docs"
description = "A small Rocdown site"

[build]
output = "dist"
assets = "assets"

[[nav]]
label = "Guide"
items = ["index", "install"]
```

Unknown keys are errors.

```sh
rocdown check .
rocdown build .
```

`check` validates links, nav ids, includes, and assets without compiling
Roc. `build` writes the output tree atomically: a failed build leaves the
previous tree in place.

## `[site]`

| Field | Default | Meaning |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `title` | `Documentation` | Header, metadata, and generated index title |
| `description` | Empty | Default page description |
| `base_url` | Empty | Canonical, sitemap, and absolute discovery URLs |
| `language` | `en` | Document language |
| `repository` | Empty | Source link in the header |
| `social_image` | Empty | Site-relative Open Graph image path |
| `favicon` | Empty | Site-relative favicon path |
| `apple_touch_icon` | Empty | Site-relative Apple touch icon path |
| `subtitle` | Empty | Short header tagline |
| `footer` | Empty | Article footer text |
| `csp` | Strict static default | Content-Security-Policy for generated HTML |

`base_url` must use HTTP or HTTPS. A trailing slash is normalized away.

`output` is resolved relative to the content root unless `--output`
overrides it. `assets` names a directory whose files are content-hashed
into `/assets/`.

## `[[nav]]`

Each item is a page ID: the content-root-relative path without
`.rocdown`.

| Source | Page ID | Route |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `index.rocdown` | `index` | `/` |
| `guides/index.rocdown` | `guides/index` | `/guides/` |
| `guides/build.rocdown` | `guides/build` | `/guides/build/` |

Unknown IDs and duplicates fail the build. Published authored pages
omitted from navigation emit `RD2202`. Use `[[nav.groups]]` under a
top-level `[[nav]]` for curated lanes. Directory landings, Overview rows,
and `RD2205` live on the
[contributor checklist](/docs/reference/contributor/checklist/).

A static catalog is Markdown, `@page`, and article blocks. Hydrate and
live pages, `service_origin`, and `--cdn-only` are
[hybrid publish](/docs/rocdown/hybrid/). Page-kind lookup is the
[language reference](/docs/rocdown/language/).

Next: [Hybrid](/docs/rocdown/hybrid/) if you need live islands, otherwise
the [language reference](/docs/rocdown/language/).
